# ============================================================
# depend.config -- tt_analog_top
#
# Format note: this is a reading of the IC Works convention, not a
# transcription of it. Align the key names with the mentor's real
# template in week 1; scripts/workspace.py parses what is here.
# ============================================================

NAME       = tt_analog_top
DOMAIN     = analog
OWNER      =
STATUS     = none
# STATUS one of: none netlist schematic layout lvs-clean signed-off

DEPENDS    = bandgap bias_gen out_buf dig_top
PROVIDES   = tt_um_bvm_mixed_signal_tile.gds

SIM        = 
TEMPLATE   = tt_analog_2x2.def  (334.88 x 225.76 um)
# Authoritative: DIEAREA ( 0 0 ) ( 334880 225760 ) at 1000
# units/um, from tt-support-tools/tech/sky130A/def/analog/.
# The 1x2 figure of 160 x 225 was wrong -- the 1x2 is
# 161.00 x 225.76, and the design needs the 2x2 anyway:
# dig_top is 8012.7 um2 of cells, and a routable macro in a
# 1x2 leaves ~81 um of height where the bandgap needs 90.
NOTE       = Places the hardened dig_top macro and every analog block.
NOTE       = Owns top-level DRC, LVS and the Tiny Tapeout precheck.
NOTE       = Metal 5 is reserved for the TT power grid: keep it clear.
NOTE       =
NOTE       = FLOORPLAN. dig_top macro 190 x 130 at the TOP-LEFT: all 43
NOTE       = digital pins sit on the top edge at y = 225.26, x 30.82 to
NOTE       = 146.74. Analog goes below and right. All 8 ua pins are on
NOTE       = the BOTTOM edge at y = 0.50, met4, 19.32 um pitch:
NOTE       =   ua[0] x=152.26  ua[1] x=132.94  ua[2] x=113.62
NOTE       =   ua[3] x=94.30   ua[4] x=74.98   ua[5] x=55.66
NOTE       =   ua[6] x=36.34   ua[7] x=17.02
NOTE       = USED: ua[0] VREF, ua[1] bias monitor. Every other ua site
NOTE       = must have NO met4 and NO via within 0.5 um of its
NOTE       = 0.9 x 1.0 um rect, or precheck's analog_pin_check fails.
NOTE       = Connect a used pin with met4 (71/20) into the 0.1-0.5 um
NOTE       = ring, or a via3 (70/44) inside the rect.
NOTE       = nwell (64/20) must stay 0.7 um clear of urpm (79/20).
